# Supabase PostgreSQL Connection String
#
# Supabase's pooler (Supavisor) caps total clients per mode:
#   - Session mode   (port 5432): pooled, hard-limited to `pool_size` (often 15).
#   - Transaction mode (port 6543): multiplexes many app connections.
#
# Prisma opens ~(2 x CPU cores + 1) connections per PrismaClient by default, so
# ALWAYS set `connection_limit` to a small value and keep a single shared client
# (see src/prisma.ts). Without this you'll hit:
#   FATAL: (EMAXCONNSESSION) max clients reached in session mode
#
# Recommended for a long-running server (session mode, works with `prisma db push`):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-eu-west-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?connection_limit=5"
#
# Alternative (transaction mode) — cheaper on connections but requires pgbouncer
# mode and does NOT work for migrations/`db push`. Use a separate direct URL:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-eu-west-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=5"

# JWT Authentication Secret
JWT_SECRET="generate_a_random_secure_string_here"

# Server Configuration
PORT=8745
